    "note": "**M2.2 — step model corrected.** All three points from your last note:\n\n**1 · Step 0 now exists.** The clip opens on **Step 0 / 8** — the unparsed canvas (just the Frame). Step 1 is the first split.\n\n**2 · Values mutate AT the split, not a step late.** The inspector now reads the *child size a split produces*, not the parent being split:\n\n| step | event | inspector |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | (idle) | full canvas `1920×1080` |\n| 1 | 2-col split | **W → 960** (halves immediately) |\n| 2 | 3-row split (left) | **H → 360** (divides by 3) |\n| 3 | first cell | paints `960×360` (no change) |\n\nThe changed field flashes its green pulse on the exact step it changes.\n\n**3 · Dashed boundaries persist.** Split dividers now stay visible the whole time and draw **on top** of the painted cells — so the structural grid builds up and never gets covered.",
    "question": "Does the step model read right now? Checks: (a) opens on Step 0 with the empty frame, (b) W halves the moment the 2-col split fires (step 1), H divides at the row split (step 2), (c) the dashed subdivision lines persist on top of the cells the whole time. If the step model + persistence are right, I'll move to **M3 — the live DSL-string panel** (syntax highlight + stepping caret + ruler + narration) which ties each value change to the symbol that caused it.",
