    "response": {
      "body": "generally good. I still want to calrify what Z is. if its just logical index, i prefer not to track that. its obvious as we write the number in the frame. Z is intended to be for OVERLAY layer level. so its 0 for ALL of these tiles. I don't think tracking logical index is that useful. tracking the overlay layer is however. step 3 and step 4 are missing a step. step 3 shows emission of a rectangle. step 4 shows emission of the next rectangle. this SKIPS a step - the COMMA. we see the x,y,W,H jump from one set of values to the other. This is NOT how m0 parses. The edits to x,y,W,H happen on the COMMA. Literally EVERY character is a step in m0. so 2(3[1,1,1],2[1,1]) is 17 STEPS. one for EVERY char. every char represents some kind of transformation to X,Y,W,H or emits a frame. open splits split the canvas. close splits restore the inspector vals. Go back to the drawing board and understand how every single char causes some kind of real step operation",
      "from": "human",
